The bug was caused by the incorrect assignment of error values, specifically setting `errno` to a negative value (e.g., `-EIO`), which could lead to unexpected behavior in error handling. This issue was introduced in a previous commit and was addressed by creating a macro to standardize the assignment of return and error values, ensuring that they are set correctly and consistently.

